 "notes": "Left page (p.124) is plain text (title + 3 printed annotation paragraphs); right page (p.125, \"CHART TWELVE\") carries the 1-date + 18-price ledger grid. Only one year appears on this spread: 1939 (Jul 15 - Aug 25); the \"1939\" figure sits in the DATE column directly above the \"DATE\" label row and is treated as yearHeader rather than a priced entry. Rows SAT.JUL.15, 19, 20, 26, 27, 28, SAT.29, 31, AUG.1-3, SAT.5, 8, SAT.12, 14-16, SAT.19, 22 have no handwritten entries and are omitted. Column assignment for the two \"60 3/8\"/\"62\" (Bethlehem) and \"50 7/8\" (US Steel) header entries was verified against the printed annotation (\"On July 21st... Bethlehem Steel recorded in Upward Trend... July 22nd... U.S. Steel recorded in Upward Trend\") which pins the black-ink UT entries to July 21 (BS=63) and July 22/Sat (US=54 1/8), leaving the blue-ink entries on rows 17/18/21 in the Natural Rally column. All KP (Key Price) readings were cross-checked against US+BS sums where all three appear same-row; two initial misreads were corrected this way: July 18 KP is 113 7/8 (not 113 1/8), and Aug 18 KP is 100 1/8 (not 100 7/8). The July 25 pivot row (US 55 1/8, BS 65 3/4, KP 120 7/8) carries a short hand-drawn underline that reads as red rather than black \u2014 distinguishable from a printed gridline because this ledger's printed red horizontal dividers fall in a fixed 6-row cadence that lands after row 28 in this block, not after row 25.",
